{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>But indeed your blood.</b> Rashi's interpretation: one who sheds his own blood — that is, lest a person say: since it was permitted to us to shed an animal's blood, given that its life is in our hands, likewise a person — his life is in his own hands, and it is permitted to kill oneself." "<b>For your souls.</b> Rashi's interpretation: even one who strangles himself — that is, even though no blood comes forth from him. An answer to those who say there is no Gehinnom and no Garden of Eden — that is, even of one who kills himself, the Holy One, blessed be He, demands his blood from him; and when, if not after death? In Breshit Rabbah: one might say, like Saul? It writes אך. One might say, like Hananiah, Mishael, and Azariah? It writes ואך. Let whoever understands, understand." "<b>From the hand of every beast I will demand it.</b> Lest a person say of his enemy: I will not kill him with my own hands, but I will throw him among wild beasts and they will kill him — therefore it says <b>from the hand of every beast I will demand it.</b> Another interpretation: <b>from the beast</b> itself <b>I will demand it</b>, as it is written, השור יסקל (the ox shall be stoned)." "<b>From the hand of man, his brother.</b> Lest one say: since it was permitted to eat living creatures, provided one does not eat them while their blood is still in them, likewise man too — it is permitted, man upon his brother, that a man may eat the flesh of his fellow and a woman the flesh of her fellow; therefore it says, from the hand of man, his brother, I will demand the life of man." "<b>I will demand.</b> Of one who kills himself or who kills his fellow in secret; but one who kills in the open — the court will exact punishment from him."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {1 "The abbreviation ת״‎ל stands for תלמוד לומר, 'the verse comes to say.' The passage alludes to a midrashic distinction between שאול (without vav) and כשאול (with vav); the Hebrew is rendered literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:03:39.111242135Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}